window.MOCK_BANK=(window.MOCK_BANK||[]).concat([{"id":"v2-61-0179","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Information security management","why":"The decisive clue matches Information security management: Protecting the information the organization needs to conduct its business. Service configuration management instead refers to providing accurate, reliable information about service configurations, supporting items and their relationships. IT asset management instead refers to managing the lifecycle of IT assets to support value, cost control, risk management and compliance.","whyNl":"De practice beschermt benodigde informatie, met aandacht voor vertrouwelijkheid, integriteit en beschikbaarheid. Alleen alles afsluiten is niet genoeg: bevoegde gebruikers moeten informatie kunnen gebruiken. Niet alleen technische maatregelen tellen. Vergelijk vooral met Service configuration management: Deze practice zorgt dat configuratie-informatie klopt en beschikbaar is wanneer nodig. Relaties tussen onderdelen zijn belangrijk voor impactanalyse. Alleen een prijslijst van apparatuur is niet genoeg.","hook":"Protect information so the business can work.","prompt":"Complete the statement: [?] is protecting the information the organization needs to conduct its business.","options":["Information security management","Service configuration management","IT asset management","Supplier management"],"kind":"missing-word","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-61-0180","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Relationship management","why":"The decisive clue matches Relationship management: Building and maintaining links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels. Supplier management instead refers to managing suppliers and their performance so they support quality service provision. Service desk instead refers to capturing demand for incident resolution and requests and acting as the users' entry point to the service provider.","whyNl":"Relationship management onderhoudt relaties en begrip op strategisch en tactisch niveau. Supplier management richt zich specifiek op leveranciers en hun prestaties. De service desk is vooral het contactpunt met gebruikers voor operationele vragen. Vergelijk vooral met Supplier management: Supplier management kijkt naar leveranciers, afspraken en prestaties om kwaliteit te ondersteunen. Dat is niet hetzelfde als alle klantrelaties onderhouden of de operationele verwerking van incidenten.","hook":"Strategic and tactical stakeholder relationships.","prompt":"Complete the statement: [?] is building and maintaining links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels.","options":["Relationship management","Supplier management","Service desk","Service level management"],"kind":"missing-word","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-61-0181","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Supplier management","why":"The decisive clue matches Supplier management: Managing suppliers and their performance so they support quality service provision. Relationship management instead refers to building and maintaining links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels. Service level management instead refers to setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them.","whyNl":"Supplier management kijkt naar leveranciers, afspraken en prestaties om kwaliteit te ondersteunen. Dat is niet hetzelfde als alle klantrelaties onderhouden of de operationele verwerking van incidenten. Vergelijk vooral met Relationship management: Relationship management onderhoudt relaties en begrip op strategisch en tactisch niveau. Supplier management richt zich specifiek op leveranciers en hun prestaties. De service desk is vooral het contactpunt met gebruikers voor operationele vragen.","hook":"Manage supplier performance.","prompt":"Complete the statement: [?] is managing suppliers and their performance so they support quality service provision.","options":["Supplier management","Relationship management","Service level management","IT asset management"],"kind":"missing-word","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-61-0182","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"IT asset management","why":"The decisive clue matches IT asset management: Managing the lifecycle of IT assets to support value, cost control, risk management and compliance. Service configuration management instead refers to providing accurate, reliable information about service configurations, supporting items and their relationships. Deployment management instead refers to moving new or changed components into live, test or staging environments.","whyNl":"IT asset management bekijkt de volledige levenscyclus en financiële waarde van IT-assets. Service configuration management richt zich op betrouwbare informatie over configuraties en relaties. Eén object kan zowel asset als CI zijn. Vergelijk vooral met Service configuration management: Deze practice zorgt dat configuratie-informatie klopt en beschikbaar is wanneer nodig. Relaties tussen onderdelen zijn belangrijk voor impactanalyse. Alleen een prijslijst van apparatuur is niet genoeg.","hook":"Asset lifecycle, value, cost and risk.","prompt":"Complete the statement: [?] is managing the lifecycle of IT assets to support value, cost control, risk management and compliance.","options":["IT asset management","Service configuration management","Deployment management","Supplier management"],"kind":"missing-word","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-61-0183","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Monitoring and event management","why":"The decisive clue matches Monitoring and event management: Observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes. Incident management instead refers to reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible. Problem management instead refers to reducing incident likelihood and impact by managing causes, workarounds and known errors.","whyNl":"Monitoring observeert de toestand; event management behandelt relevante toestandsveranderingen. Niet elk event is een incident. Een succesvolle back-upmelding kan een informatief event zijn zonder serviceverstoring. Vergelijk vooral met Incident management: Incident management richt zich op herstel. Het mag een workaround gebruiken zonder eerst de definitieve oorzaak weg te nemen. Oorzaakanalyse en structurele beheersing horen primair bij problem management.","hook":"Observe state; handle significant changes.","prompt":"Complete the statement: [?] is observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes.","options":["Monitoring and event management","Incident management","Problem management","Service configuration management"],"kind":"missing-word","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"x601","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Information security management","prompt":"Which practice protects the information an organization needs for its business, including its confidentiality, integrity and availability?","options":["Information security management","Service configuration management","IT asset management","Monitoring and event management"],"why":"Information security management protects business information. Configuration management provides information about configurations, asset management concerns asset lifecycles and value, and monitoring observes state changes.","hook":"Protect information: security. Describe components: configuration.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Informatie beschermen is information security management. Configuration management zorgt voor configuratie- en afhankelijkheidsinformatie. Asset management kijkt naar financiële waarde en levenscyclus. Monitoring observeert relevante toestandsveranderingen. Het specifieke beschermingsdoel beslist.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x602","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Relationship management","prompt":"Which practice establishes and nurtures links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels?","options":["Relationship management","Service desk","Supplier management","Service level management"],"why":"Relationship management develops stakeholder relationships broadly. The service desk is a contact point for users, supplier management focuses on suppliers and service level management agrees business-based service targets.","hook":"Stakeholder relationships beyond individual tickets.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Strategische en tactische stakeholderrelaties vormen de brede focus van relationship management. Supplier management focust specifiek op leveranciers. Service level management bepaalt servicetargets; service desk is de gebruikersingang. Allemaal contacten, maar met verschillende doelen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x603","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Supplier management","prompt":"Which practice ensures that suppliers and their performance are managed appropriately to support quality products and services?","options":["Supplier management","Relationship management","Service level management","IT asset management"],"why":"Supplier management focuses specifically on suppliers and their performance. Relationship management has broader stakeholder scope; service level management focuses on service quality targets and assessment.","hook":"Supplier performance is the key clue.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Leveranciers en hun prestaties beheren hoort bij supplier management. Relationship management is breder. Service level management spreekt af wat de service voor de business moet leveren. Asset management beheert waarde en levenscyclus van assets, niet primair leveranciersprestaties.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x604","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"IT asset management","prompt":"Which practice plans and manages the full lifecycle of IT assets to help control costs and risks and maximize value?","options":["IT asset management","Service configuration management","Deployment management","Supplier management"],"why":"Asset management addresses the lifecycle and value of financially valuable IT assets. Configuration management focuses on reliable information about service configurations and their relationships.","hook":"Asset: lifecycle, cost, risk and value.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Waarde, kosten, risico en volledige levenscyclus van IT-assets is IT asset management. Service configuration management levert betrouwbare configuratie- en relatie-informatie. Deployment verplaatst componenten. Eén component kan bij verschillende practices relevant zijn; de nadruk verschilt.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x605","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Monitoring and event management","prompt":"Which practice systematically observes services and components and records selected changes of state as events?","options":["Monitoring and event management","Incident management","Problem management","Service configuration management"],"why":"Monitoring and event management observes and handles relevant state changes. An event can be informational; incident management addresses disruption or degraded service rather than every event.","hook":"Notice the state change before deciding what it means.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Observeren, registreren en verwerken van geselecteerde relevante toestandsveranderingen is monitoring and event management. Een event is niet per definitie een verstoring. Incident management richt zich op herstel; problem management op oorzaken; configuration management op informatie over de inrichting.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x606","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Release management","prompt":"Which practice makes new or changed services and features available for use?","options":["Release management","Deployment management","Change enablement","Service configuration management"],"why":"Release management concerns availability for use. Deployment moves components into environments, while change enablement assesses risk and authorization. Installed software may not yet be released to users.","hook":"Release: available to use. Deployment: moved into place.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Beschikbaar maken voor gebruik is release management. Deployment verplaatst componenten naar een omgeving; die kunnen nog achter een uitgeschakelde feature flag staan. Change enablement beoordeelt risico en autoriseert. Deze activiteiten kunnen apart in de tijd plaatsvinden.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x607","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Service configuration management","prompt":"Which practice ensures that accurate information about service configurations, supporting items and their relationships is available when needed?","options":["Service configuration management","IT asset management","Monitoring and event management","Service level management"],"why":"Configuration management supplies trustworthy configuration information and relationships. Asset management has a financial lifecycle focus, while monitoring tracks state changes.","hook":"Configuration: what supports what?","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Betrouwbare informatie over configuraties en hun onderlinge relaties is service configuration management. IT asset management benadrukt financiële waarde en levenscyclus. Monitoring registreert events. Alleen een inventarislijst met prijzen is niet voldoende om serviceafhankelijkheden te begrijpen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x608","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Deployment management","prompt":"Which practice moves new or changed hardware, software, documentation or other components into live environments, and may also move them into test environments?","options":["Deployment management","Release management","Change enablement","IT asset management"],"why":"Deployment moves components between environments. Release makes features available for use, and change enablement assesses and authorizes changes. These purposes are related but distinct.","hook":"Deployment moves; release makes available.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Verplaatsen van nieuwe of gewijzigde componenten naar omgevingen is deployment management. Release maakt ze beschikbaar voor gebruik. Change enablement beoordeelt en autoriseert wijzigingen. Het installeren zelf is dus niet hetzelfde als toestemming of beschikbaarstelling voor gebruikers.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x609","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Continual improvement","prompt":"Which practice aligns services and working methods with changing business needs through ongoing improvements?","options":["Continual improvement","Service level management","Change enablement","Problem management"],"why":"Continual improvement has the broad purpose of ongoing alignment and improvement. Service level management sets and assesses service targets; change enablement controls changes; problem management addresses incident causes.","hook":"Keep services and working methods aligned as needs change.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Continual improvement houdt services en practices blijvend passend bij veranderende businessbehoeften. Het is breder dan incidentoorzaken onderzoeken of individuele changes autoriseren. Service level management bepaalt en bewaakt servicekwaliteitstargets; die kunnen verbeteringen helpen aanwijzen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x610","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Change enablement","prompt":"Which practice aims to increase successful product and service changes through risk assessment, authorization and schedule management?","options":["Change enablement","Release management","Deployment management","Continual improvement"],"why":"Those three responsibilities identify change enablement. Release and deployment concern making functionality available and moving components; improvement has a broader ongoing alignment purpose.","hook":"Assess, authorize and coordinate changes.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Risico beoordelen, changes autoriseren en de change schedule beheren vormen change enablement. Release maakt iets bruikbaar voor gebruikers; deployment verplaatst onderdelen. Continual improvement omvat de bredere blijvende verbetering. Eén traject kan al deze practices toepassen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x611","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Incident management","prompt":"Which purpose belongs to incident management?","options":["Reduce the impact of incidents by restoring normal service promptly","Reduce future incidents by identifying causes and managing workarounds","Observe services and record selected changes of state","Handle agreed user requests through predefined workflows"],"why":"Incident management prioritizes restoring service. Finding actual or potential causes is problem management; observing state changes is monitoring; agreed normal requests belong to service request management.","hook":"Incident management: restore service.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Incident management beperkt negatieve gevolgen via zo snel mogelijk normaal serviceherstel. Oorzaken en workarounds beheren hoort bij problem management, events observeren bij monitoring en normale aanvragen afhandelen bij request management. Herstel hoeft niet te wachten op een permanente fix.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x612","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Problem management","prompt":"Which practice reduces the likelihood and impact of incidents by identifying causes and managing workarounds and known errors?","options":["Problem management","Incident management","Monitoring and event management","Change enablement"],"why":"Problem management addresses actual and potential causes and the management of workarounds and known errors. Incident management focuses on restoring service following disruption.","hook":"Problem management: understand causes and reduce their effects.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Problem management vermindert kans en impact via oorzakenonderzoek en het beheren van workarounds en known errors. Incident management focust op actueel serviceherstel. Monitoring kan signalen leveren, maar neemt het oorzakenonderzoek niet automatisch over.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x613","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Service request management","prompt":"Which practice handles predefined, user-initiated requests as part of normal service delivery in an effective, user-friendly way?","options":["Service request management","Service desk","Incident management","Change enablement"],"why":"Service request management handles agreed normal requests through suitable workflows. The desk may receive those requests, but its purpose as a contact point is different from fulfilling them.","hook":"Receive at the desk; fulfil through request management.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Vooraf gedefinieerde normale gebruikersverzoeken effectief afhandelen is service request management. De desk kan ze ontvangen, maar ontvangst is niet de hele afhandeling. Incident management herstelt verstoringen; change enablement regelt risico en autorisatie van wijzigingen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x614","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Service desk","prompt":"Which practice captures demand for incident resolution and service requests and provides a contact point between provider and users?","options":["Service desk","Service request management","Incident management","Relationship management"],"why":"Capturing this demand and providing the user contact point are central to the service desk. Incident and request management address the work that follows; relationship management has broader stakeholder scope.","hook":"Service desk: the user's contact point.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Het centrale contactpunt en het opvangen van incident- en requestvraag zijn de service desk. De afhandeling kan andere teams en practices gebruiken. Relationship management gaat over bredere strategische en tactische stakeholderrelaties, niet specifiek deze gebruikersingang.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x615","criterion":"6.1","lo":6,"tag":"Service level management","prompt":"Which practice sets clear, business-based service targets and ensures delivery is assessed and managed against them?","options":["Service level management","Relationship management","Supplier management","Monitoring and event management"],"why":"Service level management connects agreed service quality to business needs and assesses performance. Monitoring provides observations, but does not replace agreement on meaningful service targets.","hook":"Agree what good service means, then assess it.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Service level management stelt businessgerichte servicekwaliteitstargets vast en beoordeelt de daadwerkelijke levering daartegen. Monitoring levert waarnemingen, maar bepaalt niet vanzelf wat een goed target is. Supplier management gaat over leveranciers; relationship management over bredere relaties.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-052","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"IT asset and CI","prompt":"A licensed application has financial value and must be managed to deliver a service. Which classification is supported?","options":["It can be both an IT asset and a configuration item","It must be an IT asset instead of a configuration item","It must be a configuration item instead of an IT asset","Its classification depends only on whether it is hardware or software"],"why":"The definitions overlap: financial value concerns assets and required management for delivery concerns CIs. Physical form does not make them exclusive.","whyNl":"Beide definities kunnen gelden. Financiële waarde maakt het een IT asset; moeten beheren voor servicelevering maakt het een CI. Het is geen keuze tussen hardware en software en het ene label sluit het andere niet uit.","hook":"An item can satisfy both definitions.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-053","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Known error and problem","prompt":"An investigation has been logged, but analysis of the suspected cause has not yet been performed. Which fact is still needed to describe it as a known error?","options":["The problem has been analysed and remains unresolved","The incident has received a high-priority label","A permanent change has been authorized for deployment","Several users have reported the same symptoms"],"why":"Known error requires an analysed unresolved problem. Priority, repetition or approval for a fix do not by themselves supply that analysis.","whyNl":"Een known error is een geanalyseerd, nog onopgelost problem. Logging, prioriteit of veel meldingen bewijst geen analyse. Een fix goedkeuren is evenmin de definitie. Een workaround is niet vereist om het known error te kunnen noemen.","hook":"Logged is not the same as analysed.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-054","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Event and incident","prompt":"Monitoring reports a component state change important for management. The service continues normally. What can be concluded from these facts?","options":["There is an event; an incident has not been established","There is an incident because every recorded event is a failure","There is a known error because the state change was recorded","There is a problem because service quality has been reduced"],"why":"A significant state change is an event. Normal service operation does not establish interruption or degradation, and recording an event is not analysis of a cause.","whyNl":"Het event staat vast, maar een incident niet: de service draait normaal. Registreren maakt geen known error. Er is ook geen kwaliteitsvermindering beschreven die de laatste optie ondersteunt. Kijk naar bewezen feiten, niet naar wat later misschien blijkt.","hook":"Significant state change does not necessarily mean interruption.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-055","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Change definition","prompt":"Which statement identifies a change most broadly in ITIL 4?","options":["An addition, modification or removal that may affect services directly or indirectly","Only software that has already been installed in production","Only functionality already made available to end users","An interruption that reduces the quality of normal service"],"why":"A change includes potential direct or indirect service effects and is not limited to deployed code or released functionality. Interruption defines an incident.","whyNl":"Change omvat toevoegen, wijzigen of verwijderen van iets dat services kan beïnvloeden, ook indirect. Het hoeft nog niet geïnstalleerd of vrijgegeven te zijn. Een onderbreking beschrijft een incident, niet de brede definitie van change.","hook":"Potential service effect, not just deployed software.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"v2-62-0184","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"IT asset","why":"The decisive clue matches IT asset: A financially valuable component that can contribute to delivering an IT product or service. Configuration item instead refers to a component that must be managed to deliver an IT service. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","whyNl":"Een IT-asset heeft financiële waarde en kan bijdragen aan IT-producten of -services. Een CI wordt gedefinieerd vanuit wat beheerd moet worden voor dienstverlening. Sommige zaken vallen onder beide definities. Vergelijk vooral met Configuration item: Een CI moet beheerd worden om een dienst te kunnen leveren. Dat kan technische of niet-technische informatie omvatten. De definitie draait om beheer voor servicelevering, niet alleen om de aanschafprijs.","hook":"Asset = financially valuable.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nA financially valuable component that can contribute to delivering an IT product or service.","options":["IT asset","Configuration item","Output","Service"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0185","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Event","why":"The decisive clue matches Event: A change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item. Incident instead refers to an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality. Problem instead refers to a cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","whyNl":"Een event is een relevante toestandsverandering. Het kan informatief, waarschuwend of uitzonderlijk zijn. Een event betekent dus niet automatisch dat de service is verstoord: dan moet je naar de definitie van incident kijken. Vergelijk vooral met Incident: Een incident hoeft geen volledige uitval te zijn. Een onverwachte kwaliteitsvermindering, zoals ernstige vertraging, kan ook een incident zijn. De oorzaak van de verstoring is een problem; dat is een ander begrip.","hook":"Event = significant state change.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nA change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item.","options":["Event","Incident","Problem","Change"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0186","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Configuration item","why":"The decisive clue matches Configuration item: A component that must be managed to deliver an IT service. IT asset instead refers to a financially valuable component that can contribute to delivering an IT product or service. Event instead refers to a change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item.","whyNl":"Een CI moet beheerd worden om een dienst te kunnen leveren. Dat kan technische of niet-technische informatie omvatten. De definitie draait om beheer voor servicelevering, niet alleen om de aanschafprijs. Vergelijk vooral met IT asset: Een IT-asset heeft financiële waarde en kan bijdragen aan IT-producten of -services. Een CI wordt gedefinieerd vanuit wat beheerd moet worden voor dienstverlening. Sommige zaken vallen onder beide definities.","hook":"CI = needs management for service delivery.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nA component that must be managed to deliver an IT service.","options":["Configuration item","IT asset","Event","Output"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0187","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Change","why":"The decisive clue matches Change: An addition, modification or removal that can affect services directly or indirectly. Event instead refers to a change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item. Incident instead refers to an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality.","whyNl":"Een change kan iets toevoegen, wijzigen of verwijderen en hoeft niet alleen software te betreffen. Ook een procedure of configuratie kan dienstverlening beïnvloeden. Een event is daarentegen een waargenomen toestandsverandering. Vergelijk vooral met Event: Een event is een relevante toestandsverandering. Het kan informatief, waarschuwend of uitzonderlijk zijn. Een event betekent dus niet automatisch dat de service is verstoord: dan moet je naar de definitie van incident kijken.","hook":"Add, modify or remove with a service effect.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nAn addition, modification or removal that can affect services directly or indirectly.","options":["Change","Event","Incident","Service request"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0188","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Incident","why":"The decisive clue matches Incident: An unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality. Event instead refers to a change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item. Problem instead refers to a cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","whyNl":"Een incident hoeft geen volledige uitval te zijn. Een onverwachte kwaliteitsvermindering, zoals ernstige vertraging, kan ook een incident zijn. De oorzaak van de verstoring is een problem; dat is een ander begrip. Vergelijk vooral met Event: Een event is een relevante toestandsverandering. Het kan informatief, waarschuwend of uitzonderlijk zijn. Een event betekent dus niet automatisch dat de service is verstoord: dan moet je naar de definitie van incident kijken.","hook":"Incident = interruption or degraded quality.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nAn unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality.","options":["Incident","Event","Problem","Service request"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0189","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Problem","why":"The decisive clue matches Problem: A cause or possible cause of one or more incidents. Incident instead refers to an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality. Known error instead refers to a problem that has been analysed and remains unresolved.","whyNl":"Een problem is een oorzaak of mogelijke oorzaak, niet simpelweg een groot of lang openstaand incident. Eén problem kan meerdere incidenten veroorzaken. Je kunt een problem ook herkennen voordat een incident plaatsvindt. Vergelijk vooral met Incident: Een incident hoeft geen volledige uitval te zijn. Een onverwachte kwaliteitsvermindering, zoals ernstige vertraging, kan ook een incident zijn. De oorzaak van de verstoring is een problem; dat is een ander begrip.","hook":"Problem = actual or potential cause.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nA cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","options":["Problem","Incident","Known error","Event"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0190","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Known error","why":"The decisive clue matches Known error: A problem that has been analysed and remains unresolved. Incident instead refers to an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality. Workaround instead refers to a way to reduce or remove impact while a complete resolution is not available.","whyNl":"Een known error is een geanalyseerd maar nog niet opgelost problem. Een workaround kan nuttig zijn, maar is geen voorwaarde in deze definitie. Het is niet hetzelfde als een herkend incident of een opgeloste fout. Vergelijk vooral met Incident: Een incident hoeft geen volledige uitval te zijn. Een onverwachte kwaliteitsvermindering, zoals ernstige vertraging, kan ook een incident zijn. De oorzaak van de verstoring is een problem; dat is een ander begrip.","hook":"Analysed + unresolved.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nA problem that has been analysed and remains unresolved.","options":["Known error","Incident","Workaround","Service request"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0191","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"IT asset","why":"The decisive clue matches IT asset: A financially valuable component that can contribute to delivering an IT product or service. Configuration item instead refers to a component that must be managed to deliver an IT service. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","whyNl":"Een IT-asset heeft financiële waarde en kan bijdragen aan IT-producten of -services. Een CI wordt gedefinieerd vanuit wat beheerd moet worden voor dienstverlening. Sommige zaken vallen onder beide definities. Vergelijk vooral met Configuration item: Een CI moet beheerd worden om een dienst te kunnen leveren. Dat kan technische of niet-technische informatie omvatten. De definitie draait om beheer voor servicelevering, niet alleen om de aanschafprijs.","hook":"Asset = financially valuable.","prompt":"Which statement about IT asset is CORRECT?","options":["A financially valuable component that can contribute to delivering an IT product or service.","A component that must be managed to deliver an IT service.","A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","A way for provider and consumer to co-create value by enabling desired outcomes without the consumer managing particular costs and risks."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0192","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Event","why":"The decisive clue matches Event: A change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item. Incident instead refers to an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality. Problem instead refers to a cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","whyNl":"Een event is een relevante toestandsverandering. Het kan informatief, waarschuwend of uitzonderlijk zijn. Een event betekent dus niet automatisch dat de service is verstoord: dan moet je naar de definitie van incident kijken. Vergelijk vooral met Incident: Een incident hoeft geen volledige uitval te zijn. Een onverwachte kwaliteitsvermindering, zoals ernstige vertraging, kan ook een incident zijn. De oorzaak van de verstoring is een problem; dat is een ander begrip.","hook":"Event = significant state change.","prompt":"Which statement about Event is CORRECT?","options":["A change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item.","An unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality.","A cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","An addition, modification or removal that can affect services directly or indirectly."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0193","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Configuration item","why":"The decisive clue matches Configuration item: A component that must be managed to deliver an IT service. IT asset instead refers to a financially valuable component that can contribute to delivering an IT product or service. Event instead refers to a change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item.","whyNl":"Een CI moet beheerd worden om een dienst te kunnen leveren. Dat kan technische of niet-technische informatie omvatten. De definitie draait om beheer voor servicelevering, niet alleen om de aanschafprijs. Vergelijk vooral met IT asset: Een IT-asset heeft financiële waarde en kan bijdragen aan IT-producten of -services. Een CI wordt gedefinieerd vanuit wat beheerd moet worden voor dienstverlening. Sommige zaken vallen onder beide definities.","hook":"CI = needs management for service delivery.","prompt":"Which statement about Configuration item is CORRECT?","options":["A component that must be managed to deliver an IT service.","A financially valuable component that can contribute to delivering an IT product or service.","A change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item.","A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0194","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Change","why":"The decisive clue matches Change: An addition, modification or removal that can affect services directly or indirectly. Event instead refers to a change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item. Incident instead refers to an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality.","whyNl":"Een change kan iets toevoegen, wijzigen of verwijderen en hoeft niet alleen software te betreffen. Ook een procedure of configuratie kan dienstverlening beïnvloeden. Een event is daarentegen een waargenomen toestandsverandering. Vergelijk vooral met Event: Een event is een relevante toestandsverandering. Het kan informatief, waarschuwend of uitzonderlijk zijn. Een event betekent dus niet automatisch dat de service is verstoord: dan moet je naar de definitie van incident kijken.","hook":"Add, modify or remove with a service effect.","prompt":"Which statement about Change is CORRECT?","options":["An addition, modification or removal that can affect services directly or indirectly.","A change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item.","An unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality.","A user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0195","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Incident","why":"The decisive clue matches Incident: An unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality. Event instead refers to a change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item. Problem instead refers to a cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","whyNl":"Een incident hoeft geen volledige uitval te zijn. Een onverwachte kwaliteitsvermindering, zoals ernstige vertraging, kan ook een incident zijn. De oorzaak van de verstoring is een problem; dat is een ander begrip. Vergelijk vooral met Event: Een event is een relevante toestandsverandering. Het kan informatief, waarschuwend of uitzonderlijk zijn. Een event betekent dus niet automatisch dat de service is verstoord: dan moet je naar de definitie van incident kijken.","hook":"Incident = interruption or degraded quality.","prompt":"Which statement about Incident is CORRECT?","options":["An unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality.","A change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item.","A cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","A user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0196","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Problem","why":"The decisive clue matches Problem: A cause or possible cause of one or more incidents. Incident instead refers to an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality. Known error instead refers to a problem that has been analysed and remains unresolved.","whyNl":"Een problem is een oorzaak of mogelijke oorzaak, niet simpelweg een groot of lang openstaand incident. Eén problem kan meerdere incidenten veroorzaken. Je kunt een problem ook herkennen voordat een incident plaatsvindt. Vergelijk vooral met Incident: Een incident hoeft geen volledige uitval te zijn. Een onverwachte kwaliteitsvermindering, zoals ernstige vertraging, kan ook een incident zijn. De oorzaak van de verstoring is een problem; dat is een ander begrip.","hook":"Problem = actual or potential cause.","prompt":"Which statement about Problem is CORRECT?","options":["A cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","An unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality.","A problem that has been analysed and remains unresolved.","A change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0197","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Known error","why":"The decisive clue matches Known error: A problem that has been analysed and remains unresolved. Incident instead refers to an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality. Workaround instead refers to a way to reduce or remove impact while a complete resolution is not available.","whyNl":"Een known error is een geanalyseerd maar nog niet opgelost problem. Een workaround kan nuttig zijn, maar is geen voorwaarde in deze definitie. Het is niet hetzelfde als een herkend incident of een opgeloste fout. Vergelijk vooral met Incident: Een incident hoeft geen volledige uitval te zijn. Een onverwachte kwaliteitsvermindering, zoals ernstige vertraging, kan ook een incident zijn. De oorzaak van de verstoring is een problem; dat is een ander begrip.","hook":"Analysed + unresolved.","prompt":"Which statement about Known error is CORRECT?","options":["A problem that has been analysed and remains unresolved.","An unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality.","A way to reduce or remove impact while a complete resolution is not available.","A user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0198","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"IT asset","why":"The decisive clue matches IT asset: A financially valuable component that can contribute to delivering an IT product or service. Configuration item instead refers to a component that must be managed to deliver an IT service. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","whyNl":"Een IT-asset heeft financiële waarde en kan bijdragen aan IT-producten of -services. Een CI wordt gedefinieerd vanuit wat beheerd moet worden voor dienstverlening. Sommige zaken vallen onder beide definities. Vergelijk vooral met Configuration item: Een CI moet beheerd worden om een dienst te kunnen leveren. Dat kan technische of niet-technische informatie omvatten. De definitie draait om beheer voor servicelevering, niet alleen om de aanschafprijs.","hook":"Asset = financially valuable.","prompt":"Complete the statement: [?] is a financially valuable component that can contribute to delivering an IT product or service.","options":["IT asset","Configuration item","Output","Service"],"kind":"missing-word","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-62-0199","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Event","why":"The decisive clue matches Event: A change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item. Incident instead refers to an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality. Problem instead refers to a cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","whyNl":"Een event is een relevante toestandsverandering. Het kan informatief, waarschuwend of uitzonderlijk zijn. Een event betekent dus niet automatisch dat de service is verstoord: dan moet je naar de definitie van incident kijken. Vergelijk vooral met Incident: Een incident hoeft geen volledige uitval te zijn. Een onverwachte kwaliteitsvermindering, zoals ernstige vertraging, kan ook een incident zijn. De oorzaak van de verstoring is een problem; dat is een ander begrip.","hook":"Event = significant state change.","prompt":"Complete the statement: [?] is a change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item.","options":["Event","Incident","Problem","Change"],"kind":"missing-word","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"x616","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Known error and problem","prompt":"Complete the statement: a problem that has been analysed but has not yet been resolved is a [?].","options":["Known error","Incident","Event","Change"],"why":"An analysed, unresolved problem is a known error. A workaround is useful where available, but is not required by this definition. An incident is a disruption or reduction in service quality.","hook":"Known error: analysed and still unresolved.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Known error betekent een geanalyseerd maar nog niet opgelost problem. Een workaround is geen voorwaarde in die definitie. Een incident is de verstoring zelf; een event de relevante toestandsverandering; een change een toevoeging, wijziging of verwijdering met mogelijk service-effect.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"missing-word"},{"id":"x617","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"IT asset and configuration item","prompt":"Which pairing correctly distinguishes an IT asset from a configuration item (CI)?","options":["IT asset: financially valuable component; CI: component managed to deliver a service","IT asset: component managed to deliver a service; CI: financially valuable component","IT asset: component in production; CI: component in a test environment","IT asset: physical component; CI: logical component"],"why":"An IT asset has financial value and contributes to IT service delivery. A CI is a component that needs management to deliver a service. The same component may satisfy both descriptions; neither category is limited to physical or logical items.","hook":"Asset and CI are different views that can overlap.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"IT asset benadrukt financiële waarde; CI benadrukt dat iets beheerd moet worden voor servicelevering. Een onderdeel kan beide zijn. Het onderscheid is niet hardware versus software of productie versus test. Kijk naar het criterium, niet naar de fysieke vorm.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x618","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Event and incident","prompt":"Which description defines an event?","options":["A state change that is significant for managing a service or configuration item","An unplanned service interruption or reduction in service quality","An actual or potential cause of one or more incidents","An addition, modification or removal that may affect services"],"why":"An event is a significant change of state. The other choices describe an incident, a problem and a change. An event does not necessarily indicate service failure.","hook":"Event means significant state change, not automatically failure.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een event is een beheersmatig relevante toestandsverandering. De andere beschrijvingen betreffen incident, problem en change. Een event kan informeren zonder dat een service verslechtert. Een melding alleen bewijst dus geen incident of geanalyseerde oorzaak.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x619","criterion":"6.2","lo":6,"tag":"Change","prompt":"Which description defines a change?","options":["An addition, modification or removal that can affect services directly or indirectly","Movement of a new or modified component into a live environment","A new or modified service or feature becoming available for use","An unexpected interruption or reduction in the quality of a service"],"why":"A change includes additions, modifications and removals with possible service effects. Deployment and release are more specific concepts; an incident is disruption or degraded quality.","hook":"Change includes indirect effects and removals too.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een change is breder dan deployment of release: toevoegen, wijzigen of verwijderen van iets dat direct of indirect services kan beïnvloeden. Een incident is ongeplande verstoring of kwaliteitsvermindering. De wijziging hoeft nog niet in productie te staan om een change te zijn.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-056","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Improvement targets and plans","prompt":"The team knows current waiting time and agrees that it should fall to two days within three months. It has not yet chosen actions. Which step is it completing?","options":["Where do we want to be?","How do we get there?","Where are we now?","Did we get there?"],"why":"The team is specifying a measurable future state. Planning the route needs actions and resources; a baseline or evaluation describes different measurements.","whyNl":"Twee dagen binnen drie maanden is de gewenste meetbare situatie. De route is nog niet gekozen, dus niet How do we get there? De huidige wachttijd is de nulmeting; achteraf toetsen is Did we get there? Het woord termijn maakt een target nog geen plan.","hook":"A target describes the destination, not the route.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-057","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Improvement plans and action","prompt":"A team agrees the target, then selects which tasks to perform and which resources each task needs. No tasks have been carried out. Which step is this?","options":["How do we get there?","Take action","Where do we want to be?","How do we keep the momentum going?"],"why":"Selecting and organizing the work is planning how to reach the target. Execution, defining the target and sustaining achieved gains have different purposes.","whyNl":"Werk kiezen en middelen plannen is de route uitwerken. Take action is het daadwerkelijke uitvoeren. Het target ligt al vast, dus Where do we want to be? is niet de huidige handeling. Er is ook nog geen bereikt resultaat om vast te houden.","hook":"Selecting actions is still planning them.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-058","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Baseline and evaluation","prompt":"The same performance measure is used before and after an improvement. Which pairing correctly distinguishes the model steps?","options":["Initial baseline: Where are we now?; result compared with target: Did we get there?","Initial baseline: Did we get there?; result compared with target: Where are we now?","Initial baseline: What is the vision?; result compared with target: Take action","Initial baseline: Where do we want to be?; result compared with target: How do we get there?"],"why":"Measurement is not unique to one step. Its purpose distinguishes establishing the starting point from evaluating the achieved result.","whyNl":"Beide stappen gebruiken metingen. Het doel maakt het verschil: vertrekpunt bepalen is Where are we now?; na uitvoering het resultaat aan de doelstelling toetsen is Did we get there? Alleen het woord meten herkennen is onvoldoende.","hook":"Ask why the measurement is being made.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-059","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Vision and targets","prompt":"Before setting a numerical target, the team checks which organizational objective an improvement will support. Which step does this illustrate?","options":["What is the vision?","Where do we want to be?","How do we get there?","Did we get there?"],"why":"Connecting improvement with organizational direction belongs to vision. A measurable future state, route and evaluation come from other questions.","whyNl":"De organisatierichting verklaart waarom de verbetering relevant is. Dat hoort bij vision. Een concreet meetbaar eindpunt is het toekomsttarget; een aanpak is de route. Hier is nog niets uitgevoerd om te evalueren.","hook":"Direction explains why the destination matters.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-060","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Keeping momentum","prompt":"An improvement has met its target. Which action most directly helps keep the momentum going?","options":["Reinforce the successful habits and continue seeking further improvements","Create the initial baseline for the same completed improvement","Select a target while disregarding the achieved result","Treat the successful project as the end of improvement responsibility"],"why":"Momentum concerns sustaining and building on gains. Measurement and target selection remain useful, but the described improvement already achieved its target.","whyNl":"Na bevestigd succes wil je resultaat vasthouden en verder leren. Niet doen alsof de eerste nulmeting nog ontbreekt, eerdere resultaten negeren of verbetering als afgesloten verantwoordelijkheid zien. Succes borgen is een expliciete stap.","hook":"Sustain the gain and keep improving.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-061","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Improvement register","prompt":"An employee records an improvement idea in a continual improvement register. What does that entry establish?","options":["An opportunity is captured for assessment and prioritization","The implementation is authorized for immediate execution","The desired outcome has already been achieved","The risk assessment for the resulting change is complete"],"why":"Recording an opportunity is not approval, implementation or proof of success. The register supports managing improvement opportunities.","whyNl":"Registreren betekent dat het idee wordt vastgelegd om te beoordelen en prioriteren. Het is geen automatische toestemming, geen gerealiseerd resultaat en geen afgeronde change-risicobeoordeling. Die stappen vragen afzonderlijke beslissingen en bewijs.","hook":"Recorded does not mean approved.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-062","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Improvement responsibilities","prompt":"Which TWO statements are correct?\n1. Staff outside a dedicated improvement team can contribute improvement ideas.\n2. Improvement work can be supported by a dedicated team.\n3. Creating a dedicated team removes improvement responsibility from everyone else.\n4. Only changes involving new technology can be improvements.","options":["1 and 2","1 and 3","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"Improvement involves everyone and can be coordinated by specialists. It applies to services, practices and other elements, not only new technology.","whyNl":"1 en 2 zijn juist: iedereen kan bijdragen en een gespecialiseerd team kan ondersteunen. 3 schuift ten onrechte alle verantwoordelijkheid weg. 4 beperkt verbetering ten onrechte tot technologie; ook werkwijzen, samenwerking en services kunnen verbeteren.","hook":"Shared responsibility with coordinated support.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"contrast-063","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Standard and normal changes","prompt":"A familiar update is low risk but the proposed version falls outside the pre-authorized procedure. There is no emergency. How should it be handled?","options":["Assess, schedule and authorize it through an appropriate normal-change route","Treat it as standard because it is familiar and low risk","Treat it as emergency because the procedure does not cover it","Proceed under the old authorization and record the variation afterwards"],"why":"Standard status depends on the authorized model and conditions, not only familiarity or risk. A change outside those conditions needs suitable assessment and authorization.","whyNl":"Een bekende laagrisicotaak is niet automatisch standaard. Deze uitvoering valt buiten de vooraf toegestane voorwaarden. Zonder spoed gebruik je passende normale beoordeling en autorisatie. Een ontbrekend model maakt het geen emergency en de oude toestemming dekt de afwijking niet.","hook":"Pre-authorization has defined boundaries.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-064","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Emergency changes","prompt":"An emergency update is needed urgently. Which approach is appropriate?","options":["Use suitably expedited assessment and authorization","Omit assessment because speed makes the risk acceptable","Use pre-authorization simply because the work is urgent","Always wait for the next routine approval meeting"],"why":"Urgency changes the handling speed and controls needed, but it does not itself remove risk or create pre-authorization.","whyNl":"Spoed vraagt een passende versnelde route. Risico verdwijnt niet omdat het snel moet en urgentie levert geen voorafgaande toestemming op. Altijd wachten op een normale vergadering kan onaanvaardbare schade laten voortduren.","hook":"Expedited does not mean uncontrolled.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-065","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change authority","prompt":"What should primarily determine the appropriate change authority?","options":["The change type and level of risk under the agreed approach","The technical experience of the implementer regardless of authorization limits","The service ownership title without considering the change model","A requirement that every change use the same senior committee"],"why":"Different change models and risk levels can need different authorizing people or groups. Consistency does not require one committee for all changes.","whyNl":"De juiste authority hangt af van het soort wijziging, risico en afgesproken werkwijze. Technische ervaring alleen geeft geen autorisatie en de functietitel alleen bepaalt niet het passende niveau. Eén zeer senior commissie voor alles is ook geen ITIL-eis. De authority kan een persoon of groep zijn.","hook":"Appropriate authority, not automatically the biggest committee.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-066","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change schedule","prompt":"Two authorized changes use the same service window. What does the change schedule primarily help the teams do?","options":["Coordinate timing and identify possible conflicts","Replace the authorization decisions with one diary entry","Prove that each implementation will succeed","Remove the need for service-impact assessment"],"why":"A schedule provides visibility and coordination. It is not authorization, a guarantee of success or a substitute for risk and impact assessment.","whyNl":"De schedule maakt overlap zichtbaar zodat teams kunnen afstemmen. Een kalenderitem is geen autorisatie of bewijs van succesvol testen. Risico en impact blijven relevant, ook als beide wijzigingen afzonderlijk zijn goedgekeurd.","hook":"Scheduling supports coordination, not permission or proof.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-067","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident and problem closure","prompt":"A workaround restores normal service and the restoration is confirmed. Investigation of the cause continues. What is the best interpretation?","options":["The incident can be resolved while the problem remains under investigation","The incident and problem must remain unresolved until a permanent fix exists","The workaround converts the incident into a service request","Confirmed restoration proves the underlying cause has been eliminated"],"why":"Incident management aims at restored normal operation. That can occur before a permanent cause resolution, subject to appropriate confirmation and closure procedures.","whyNl":"Een incident kan opgelost zijn na bevestigd serviceherstel, terwijl problem management doorzoekt. De workaround bewijst geen definitieve oorzaaksoplossing. Het wordt evenmin een service request. Volg wel de afgesproken bevestigings- en afsluitprocedure.","hook":"Restore the service; keep managing the cause.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-068","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident prioritization","prompt":"An incident blocks a critical deadline for ten users; another affects a less urgent task for more users. What should guide priority?","options":["Agreed assessment of business impact and urgency","Number of affected users without considering the business activity","Which technical team can claim the quickest closure","The order of reports regardless of changes in impact"],"why":"Impact and urgency reflect business consequences. User count, effort and arrival order provide context but are not sufficient alone.","whyNl":"Kijk naar bedrijfsimpact en urgentie. Aantallen kunnen impact helpen beoordelen, maar bepalen niet zelfstandig de prioriteit. Een kritieke deadline voor een kleine groep kan zwaarder wegen. Snel kunnen sluiten of als eerste melden is geen volledige prioriteringsgrond.","hook":"Impact and urgency, not just volume.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-069","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident collaboration","prompt":"The first support team cannot restore a disrupted service with its current knowledge. Which response best supports incident management?","options":["Bring in relevant expertise while keeping restoration and communication coordinated","Keep the incident with that team until it discovers the root cause","Close the incident when a specialist accepts the investigation","Reclassify the disruption as a problem so restoration can wait"],"why":"Incident management can coordinate specialists and suppliers. Handover or root-cause investigation is not itself restored service.","whyNl":"Schakel geschikte expertise in en houd herstel en communicatie gecoördineerd. Een overdracht is geen herstel. Wachten op root cause of de classificatie veranderen mag niet het echte doel verdringen: normale service zo snel mogelijk terugbrengen.","hook":"Escalation supports restoration; it does not equal restoration.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-070","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Proactive problem management","prompt":"A supplier identifies a defect likely to cause future interruptions, but it has not yet caused an incident here. What is appropriate?","options":["Assess it as a potential problem and consider reducing the risk","Wait for an incident because potential causes cannot be problems","Record a resolved incident because no interruption is currently visible","Call it a known error solely because the supplier mentioned it"],"why":"A problem can be a potential cause. Its analysis and unresolved status determine known-error classification; no actual interruption has been established.","whyNl":"Een mogelijke oorzaak valt onder problem. Je hoeft niet op de eerste verstoring te wachten. Er is geen opgelost incident beschreven. Een melding door een supplier bewijst op zichzelf ook niet dat de analyse voor een known error gereed is.","hook":"Potential causes count too.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-071","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Known errors without workarounds","prompt":"A problem has been analysed and is still unresolved, but no workaround is available. Which statement is correct?","options":["It can be a known error without a workaround","It becomes a known error only after a workaround is documented","It cannot be a problem until normal service has been restored","It must be a normal change because analysis has finished"],"why":"Analysis plus unresolved status satisfies the known-error definition. A workaround is a possible way to limit effects, not a definitional prerequisite.","whyNl":"Geanalyseerd en nog onopgelost is voldoende. Een workaround helpt tegen de gevolgen, maar is geen voorwaarde. Een problem vereist ook niet eerst herstel. Afronding van analyse verandert de oorzaak niet automatisch in een change.","hook":"Known error: analysed, unresolved.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-072","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Managing unresolved problems","prompt":"The cost of a permanent solution exceeds the expected benefit and an effective workaround exists. What should the organization do?","options":["Assess residual risk and keep the unresolved problem and workaround under review","Mark the cause as permanently removed because users can work","Require a permanent solution regardless of costs or benefits","Stop collecting related information once the workaround is recorded"],"why":"Not every problem justifies immediate permanent correction. Costs, risks and benefits should be assessed while the unresolved condition remains managed.","whyNl":"Een definitieve oplossing hoeft niet altijd direct rendabel te zijn. Beheer het resterende risico en blijf de workaround en het problem volgen. Bruikbare omweg betekent niet dat de oorzaak weg is. Registratie is geen reden om niet meer te monitoren of beoordelen.","hook":"Accepting residual risk still requires management.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-073","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service request approval","prompt":"A routine access request requires a manager's approval in its request model. How should it be fulfilled?","options":["Follow the predefined workflow, including the approval","Skip the approval because routine requests are always pre-authorized","Treat it as an incident because the access is not yet provided","Classify it as a problem because approval is a potential delay"],"why":"Predefined requests can include approvals. Routine fulfilment does not bypass authorization or turn a normal request into a disruption or cause.","whyNl":"Normale service requests mogen goedkeuringen bevatten. Het request model bepaalt de route. Routine betekent niet automatisch vooraf geautoriseerd. Nog geen nieuw recht hebben is ook niet zonder meer een verstoring van een bestaande service.","hook":"Predefined does not mean approval-free.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-074","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Requests and standard changes","prompt":"An agreed laptop request is fulfilled using a documented pre-authorized installation procedure. Which relationship is correct?","options":["Request management can coordinate fulfilment that includes a standard change","The installation removes the need for request management","Any user request makes the included change an emergency","A standard change must be re-authorized as normal each time it fulfils a request"],"why":"Practices can work together; a request can include a change executed within a pre-authorized model. The two classifications describe different aspects.","whyNl":"Request management behandelt het verzoek. Een standard change kan onderdeel zijn van die afhandeling, binnen toegestane voorwaarden. De practices vervangen elkaar niet. Een gebruikersverzoek maakt niets automatisch spoed of een normal change.","hook":"One request can include work from several practices.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-075","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service desk capability","prompt":"Routine work is automated and the remaining user contacts are more complex. Which capability is especially important for the service desk?","options":["Communication, empathy and understanding of the user's business context","Routing every contact without understanding what the user needs","Taking responsibility for every specialist resolution personally","Reducing conversation duration even when understanding is incomplete"],"why":"The desk remains the human contact point and needs to understand people and business context. Automation does not make empathy or coordination obsolete.","whyNl":"Juist de resterende complexe gesprekken vragen begrip, communicatie en empathie. De desk hoeft niet alles zelf technisch op te lossen. Blind routeren of gespreksduur verkorten terwijl de hulpvraag onduidelijk blijft, ondersteunt de gebruiker niet goed.","hook":"Automation leaves human understanding important.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-076","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service measures","prompt":"All component dashboards are green, but users cannot finish their business transactions within the agreed time. What should service level management do?","options":["Review end-to-end service performance and the appropriateness of the measures","Declare the service successful because each component met its own target","Replace customer feedback with a larger set of component counters","Transfer the business-outcome concern entirely to the supplier"],"why":"Component results can conceal poor end-to-end service. Targets and measures should reflect meaningful business-based service quality.","whyNl":"Groene componentcijfers bewijzen geen goede volledige service. Onderzoek de klantreis en of targets de relevante businesskwaliteit meten. Meer technische tellers vervangen gebruikerservaring niet. Verantwoordelijkheid volledig afschuiven helpt evenmin.","hook":"Component green can hide service red.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-077","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level agreements","prompt":"Which TWO characteristics support a useful service level agreement?\n1. Targets are linked to business needs.\n2. The wording is understandable to the relevant parties.\n3. Component measures replace discussion of the whole service.\n4. Every provider measure becomes a target regardless of relevance.","options":["1 and 2","1 and 3","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"Business relevance and mutual understanding support useful agreements. A catalogue of technical measures is not automatically a meaningful service commitment.","whyNl":"1 en 2 zijn juist. Doelen moeten betekenis hebben voor de business en begrijpelijk zijn voor de betrokkenen. 3 vervangt de hele service door onderdelen. 4 maakt alles meetbaar belangrijk, ook als het geen relevante serviceafspraak ondersteunt.","hook":"Business-based and understood by both sides.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"v2-71-0020","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement","prompt":"A team repeatedly checks where its services and practices could better support changing business needs and records opportunities for action.\nWhich practice BEST fits this situation?","options":["Continual improvement","Service level management","Change enablement","Problem management"],"why":"The decisive clue matches Continual improvement: Keeping services and practices aligned with changing business needs through ongoing improvement. Service level management instead refers to setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them. Change enablement instead refers to increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","whyNl":"Continual improvement brengt diensten en werkwijzen steeds in lijn met veranderende behoeften. Het is geen eenmalig groot project en niet alleen de taak van één manager. Verbeteringen kunnen klein zijn en op elk niveau ontstaan. Vergelijk vooral met Service level management: Service level management maakt bedrijfsgerichte doelen en bewaakt levering daartegen. Alleen technische componentmetingen zijn geen volledig beeld. Gesprekken met klanten en gebruikers helpen om prestaties en ervaring te begrijpen.","hook":"Keep alignment as needs change.","kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0021","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement","prompt":"Improvement work is treated as an ongoing responsibility rather than a one-off project owned by a specialist team.\nWhich practice BEST fits this situation?","options":["Continual improvement","Service level management","Change enablement","Problem management"],"why":"The decisive clue matches Continual improvement: Keeping services and practices aligned with changing business needs through ongoing improvement. Service level management instead refers to setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them. Change enablement instead refers to increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","whyNl":"Continual improvement brengt diensten en werkwijzen steeds in lijn met veranderende behoeften. Het is geen eenmalig groot project en niet alleen de taak van één manager. Verbeteringen kunnen klein zijn en op elk niveau ontstaan. Vergelijk vooral met Service level management: Service level management maakt bedrijfsgerichte doelen en bewaakt levering daartegen. Alleen technische componentmetingen zijn geen volledig beeld. Gesprekken met klanten en gebruikers helpen om prestaties en ervaring te begrijpen.","hook":"Keep alignment as needs change.","kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0022","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement","prompt":"A team uses a structured model to move from a shared vision and baseline to action, evaluation and sustained momentum.\nWhich practice BEST fits this situation?","options":["Continual improvement","Service level management","Change enablement","Problem management"],"why":"The decisive clue matches Continual improvement: Keeping services and practices aligned with changing business needs through ongoing improvement. Service level management instead refers to setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them. Change enablement instead refers to increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","whyNl":"Continual improvement brengt diensten en werkwijzen steeds in lijn met veranderende behoeften. Het is geen eenmalig groot project en niet alleen de taak van één manager. Verbeteringen kunnen klein zijn en op elk niveau ontstaan. Vergelijk vooral met Service level management: Service level management maakt bedrijfsgerichte doelen en bewaakt levering daartegen. Alleen technische componentmetingen zijn geen volledig beeld. Gesprekken met klanten en gebruikers helpen om prestaties en ervaring te begrijpen.","hook":"Keep alignment as needs change.","kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0023","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change enablement","prompt":"A proposed modification is assessed for risk and then sent to the appropriate authority before implementation is scheduled.\nWhich practice BEST fits this situation?","options":["Change enablement","Deployment management","Release management","Continual improvement"],"why":"The decisive clue matches Change enablement: Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule. Deployment management instead refers to moving new or changed components into live, test or staging environments. Release management instead refers to making new or changed services and features available for use.","whyNl":"Change enablement helpt changes succesvol te laten verlopen met passende risicoafweging, autorisatie en planning. Het doel is niet alle changes blokkeren. De juiste authority hangt af van type en risico. Vergelijk vooral met Deployment management: Deployment is het verplaatsen van componenten naar een omgeving. Het kan om software, hardware of documentatie gaan, en niet uitsluitend productie. Beschikbaar stellen voor gebruik is release management.","hook":"Assess risk, authorize, coordinate.","kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0024","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change enablement","prompt":"Different change models use different authorities, and the schedule is used to help avoid conflicts between planned changes.\nWhich practice BEST fits this situation?","options":["Change enablement","Deployment management","Release management","Continual improvement"],"why":"The decisive clue matches Change enablement: Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule. Deployment management instead refers to moving new or changed components into live, test or staging environments. Release management instead refers to making new or changed services and features available for use.","whyNl":"Change enablement helpt changes succesvol te laten verlopen met passende risicoafweging, autorisatie en planning. Het doel is niet alle changes blokkeren. De juiste authority hangt af van type en risico. Vergelijk vooral met Deployment management: Deployment is het verplaatsen van componenten naar een omgeving. Het kan om software, hardware of documentatie gaan, en niet uitsluitend productie. Beschikbaar stellen voor gebruik is release management.","hook":"Assess risk, authorize, coordinate.","kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0025","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change enablement","prompt":"The organization aims to increase the number of successful service changes while balancing risk and speed.\nWhich practice BEST fits this situation?","options":["Change enablement","Deployment management","Release management","Continual improvement"],"why":"The decisive clue matches Change enablement: Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule. Deployment management instead refers to moving new or changed components into live, test or staging environments. Release management instead refers to making new or changed services and features available for use.","whyNl":"Change enablement helpt changes succesvol te laten verlopen met passende risicoafweging, autorisatie en planning. Het doel is niet alle changes blokkeren. De juiste authority hangt af van type en risico. Vergelijk vooral met Deployment management: Deployment is het verplaatsen van componenten naar een omgeving. Het kan om software, hardware of documentatie gaan, en niet uitsluitend productie. Beschikbaar stellen voor gebruik is release management.","hook":"Assess risk, authorize, coordinate.","kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true}]);
